etween 6300 and 10000Ft; Wet Mountains above 10000 Ft; Pueblo Vicinity/Pueblo County Below 6300 Feet","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.756c47587b9063b4ff8ae253c038ec09a9c93d18.002.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.756c47587b9063b4ff8ae253c038ec09a9c93d18.002.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued August 15 at 4:59PM MDT until August 15 at 10:00PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flash flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of central, east central, and southeast Colorado,\nincluding the following areas, Teller, El Paso, Huerfano, Las\nAnimas, Crowley, Otero, Kiowa, Bent and Prowers Counties.\n\n* WHEN...Until 10 PM MDT this evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Abundant monsoon moisture will result in scattered to numerous\nthunderstorms this afternoon and evening which will be capable of\nproducing heavy rainfall and flash flooding, especially for urban\nareas or locations with already saturated soil conditions.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-08-15T22:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Teller County/Rampart Range above 7500fT/Pike's Peak Between 7500 And 11000 Ft; Pikes Peak above 11000 Ft; Northern El Paso County/Monument Ridge/Rampart Range Below 7500 Ft; Colorado Springs Vicinity/Southern El Paso County/Rampart Range Below 7400 Ft; Walsenburg Vicinity/Upper Huerfano River Basin Below 7500 Ft; Trinidad Vicinity/Western Las Animas County Below 7500 Ft; Crowley County; La Junta Vicinity/Otero County; Eastern Las Animas County; Western Kiowa County; Eastern Kiowa County; Las Animas Vicinity/Bent County; Lamar Vicinity/Prowers County","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.756c47587b9063b4ff8ae253c038ec09a9c93d18.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.756c47587b9063b4ff8ae253c038ec09a9c93d18.001.1"},{"event":"Flash Flood Watch","headline":"Flash Flood Watch issued August 15 at 4:59PM MDT until August 16 at 8:00PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flash flooding and debris flows caused by excessive rainfall\ncontinue to be possible over the Aspen Acres burn scar.\n\n* WHERE...Aspen Acres Burn Scar\n\n* WHEN...Until 8 PM MDT this evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Heavy rainfall over the Aspen Acres burn scar is expected\nup to and during the period of the watch. Residents near the Aspen\nAcres burn scar should prepare for potential debris flow. Be sure\nto stay up to date with information from local authorities. Heavy\nrainfall could trigger flash flooding of low-lying areas, street\nflooding, and debris flows in and near recent wildfire burn scars.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- National Weather Service Meteorologists are forecasting\nthunderstorms with heavy rainfall over the burn scar, which may\nlead to flash flooding and debris flows.\n- Some locations that may experience flash flooding include...\nBeulah, San Isabel, and highways 165 and 78 in and around the\nAspen Acres Burn Scar.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-08-16T20:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Wet Mountains between 6300 and 10000Ft; Wet Mountains above 10000 Ft; Pueblo Vicinity/Pueblo County Below 6300 Feet","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.756c47587b9063b4ff8ae253c038ec09a9c93d18.002.2","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.756c47587b9063b4ff8ae253c038ec09a9c93d18.002.2"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-08-15T23:41:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 152341 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 541 PM MDT Sat Aug 15 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Thunderstorms capable of producing heavy rainfall and flash flooding continue through Sunday with a few strong to severe thunderstorms across the southeast plains both days. - Thunderstorm activity a little less widespread for Monday as drier air works in 